op: Intl.Segmenter word segments, their indices
in: str:"\u00AD\u0308\u24C2" str:"word"
out: value: str:"0,2"
class: impl-defined
per-engine.broiler-js: value: str:"0,2"
per-engine.broiler-vm: value: str:"0,2"
divergence.broiler-js: row G2: Broiler.JS's word boundaries are not UAX #29's (a word is not broken at an apostrophe, an underscore, a full stop between letters or a comma between digits, and each ideograph is a word); SJL-7.5 corrects it
prov: ref:unicoderef@1 ucd:17.0.0/WordBreakTest.txt ucd:17.0.0/WordBreakProperty.txt ucd:17.0.0/emoji-data.txt
script: Array.from(new Intl.Segmenter("en", { granularity: "word" }).segment("\u00AD\u0308\u24C2"), function (s) { return s.index; }).join()
note: WordBreakTest.txt line 280. UAX #29's default boundaries, out and both engines' plans: Broiler.VM's JSD-0074 decision 1, Broiler.JS's docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md record of SJL-7.1
since: 18

