in: str:" \u00AD" str:"word"
out: value: str:"N"
class: impl-defined
per-engine.broiler-js: value: str:"N"
per-engine.broiler-vm: value: str:"N"
divergence.broiler-js: rows G2 and G4: Broiler.JS's word segments are not UAX #29's (row G2), and with them each segment's isWordLike, which is implementation-defined (row G4) and which the vector's broiler-js expectation reads as the owner's word status; SJL-7.5 corrects it
prov: ref:unicoderef@1 ucd:17.0.0/WordBreakProperty.txt ucd:17.0.0/PropList.txt ucd:17.0.0/Scripts.txt
script: Array.from(new Intl.Segmenter("en", { granularity: "word" }).segment(" \u00AD"), function (s) { return s.isWordLike ? "Y" : "N"; }).join("")
note: WordBreakTest.txt line 1175's segments. The owner's word status (row G4), out and both engines' plans: Broiler.VM's JSD-0074 (X2, G4), Broiler.JS's docs/roadmap/SharedLibraries.md record of SJL-7.1
since: 18

id: unicode/segmenter-word/1150
area: unicode
